    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID43",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_7e807ac03d0890a138fee7b9__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.1 threats of harm – Expressing intent, willingness or desire to harm an individual woman or group of women. This could include, but is not limited to: physical, sexual, emotional or privacy-based forms of harm.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Cyber harassment and bullying can involve unwanted, sexually explicit messages and threats of violence. It can also take the form of a persistent and repeated course of conduct targeted at a specific person, designed to cause severe emotional distress and often a fear of physical harm. Perpetrators are often anonymous and may target women with threats and/or fantasies of sexual violence.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
