    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID47",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_7de4eb5b4f67f3549331af84__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.2 incitement and encouragement of harm – Inciting or encouraging an individual, group, or general audience to harm a woman or group of women. It includes language where the author seeks to rationalise and/or justify harming women to another person.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech includes content posted and shared through ICT means that spreads, incites, promotes, or justifies hatred based on gender or a combination of gender and other factors such as race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion, or profession. It can also involve posting and sharing violent content that portrays women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence, whether privately or publicly, and is often targeted at women in public-facing roles. Such acts can start online and continue offline or start offline and continue online, and can be perpetrated by unknown individuals or groups or by people known to the victim.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
