    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID58",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_17b20afbcbbf292d1aa8d574__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Illustrative Gender Stereotypes and Gender Discriminatory Roles\n\nWomen as hypersexualised, and their bodies for the pleasure and spectacle of men.\n\nDouble standards regarding nudity:\n - Censorship of women’s bodies which are considered sexualised and indecent as compared to men’s, especially on social media and online platforms.\n - Women’s bodies expected to meet specific beauty standards but considered lewd in their natural state (e.g. during menstruation, showing bodily hair, breastfeeding, diverse body shapes and skin colours).\n\nPolicing of women and girl’s clothing and the idea that certain styles of dress are distracting to men and boys.\n\nBlaming and/or stigmatization and shaming of sexual violence survivors, and women and girls who report sexual violence as promiscuous, liars or ‘out to get’ the perpetrator.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender stereotypes hypersexualise women and frame their bodies as objects for men’s pleasure and spectacle. Gendered double standards treat women’s bodies as sexualised and indecent compared with men’s, subject them to censorship on online platforms, and demand specific beauty standards while labelling natural bodily states and diversity as lewd. Women’s and girls’ clothing is policed as distracting to men and boys, while sexual violence survivors and those who report sexual violence face blame, stigma, and characterisations as promiscuous, liars, or intent on harming the perpetrator.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_17b20afbcbbf292d1aa8d574__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
        "SubSelector": "TX",
