      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID67",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_03621246730498e7cf0f3431__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech expresses contempt based on sex or gender, treats a person as inferior or reduces them to their sexual dimension, and includes expressions that spread, incite, promote or justify sex-based hatred. Online and offline forms include victim blaming, slut-shaming, body-shaming and offensive comments about appearance, sexuality, sexual orientation or gender roles; supposed jokes and false compliments can also be used to humiliate and ridicule targets. Its true extent is partly hidden because many targeted women do not report it.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_03621246730498e7cf0f3431__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
