    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID70",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_dada9eaf6afdfff4ad92be91__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">4. Towards common definitions of cyber violence against women and girls &gt; How is cyber bullying linked to offline violence and vice versa? &gt; What is online gender-based hate speech?\n\nOnline hate speech is an umbrella-term commonly employed to describe any form of vitriol, libel or offensive remarks directed at another user using ICT, including on social media platforms, messaging apps and discussion sites. Online social media platforms, in particular, have been shown to expand aggressors’ means of sending hateful messages to users both known and unknown to them (De Vido and Sosa, 2021). Attacks on a person or group are largely on the grounds of one or more of their personal characteristics, such as race, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin or religion (Costello and Hawdon, 2020).\n\nOnline gender-based hate speech, in particular, targets women, girls and LGBTIQ+ individuals because of their gender. It often takes the form of sexualisation, objectification, body shaming or</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech targets women, girls and LGBTIQ+ individuals because of their gender and can take the form of sexualisation, objectification and body shaming. Online hate speech includes vitriol, libel and offensive remarks delivered through digital communication technologies. Social media platforms expand aggressors’ means of sending hateful messages to people both known and unknown to them.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_dada9eaf6afdfff4ad92be91__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
