      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech targets women, girls and LGBTIQ+ individuals because of their gender and can take the form of sexualisation, objectification and body shaming. Online hate speech includes vitriol, libel and offensive remarks delivered through digital communication technologies. Social media platforms expand aggressors’ means of sending hateful messages to people both known and unknown to them.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
