        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online hate speech includes vitriol, libel, or offensive remarks directed at users through information and communication technologies, including social media platforms, messaging apps, and discussion sites. Social media platforms expand aggressors’ means of sending hateful messages to users both known and unknown to them. Online gender-based hate speech targets women, girls, and LGBTIQ+ individuals because of their gender and often takes the form of sexualisation, objectification, or body shaming.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
