      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.1 casual use of gendered slurs, profanities, and insults – Using gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and insults, but not to intentionally attack women. Only terms that traditionally describe women are in scope (e.g. ‘b*tch’, ‘sl*t’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">National components of online gender-based hate speech vary: some include calumny, defamation and insults as a conduct category, while others include sexism. Intentional acts and effects on victims are separately identified variables in some national entries. These categories do not establish whether casual use of woman-directed slurs without intent to attack women is covered.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
