    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID98",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_b63eb0e9929946c80df3ee73__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Causes and forms of sexist hate speech\n\nSexist hate speech is one of the expressions of sexism, which can be defined as any supposition, belief, assertion, gesture or act that is aimed at expressing contempt towards a person, based on her or his sex or gender, or to consider that person as inferior or essentially reduced to her or his sexual dimension. Sexist hate speech includes expressions which spread, incite, promote or justify hatred based on sex. The true extent of sexist hate speech is partly hidden by the fact that many targeted women do not report it.\n\nPrevalence of sexual harassment among women (%, European Union, 2014)\n</div><table><tr><th>Period</th><th>Prevalence (%)</th></tr>\n<tr><th>In the last 12 months</th><td>21</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Since the age of 15</th><td>55</td></tr></table><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">\nSexist hate speech takes many forms both online and offline, notably victim blaming and re-victimisation; “slut-shaming”; body-shaming; “revenge porn” (the sharing of explicit or sexual images without consent); brutal and sexualised threats of death, rape and violence; offensive comments on appearance, sexuality, sexual orientation or gender roles; but also false compliments or supposed jokes, using humour to humiliate and ridicule the target.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism includes beliefs, assertions, gestures or acts that express contempt toward someone based on sex or gender, treat that person as inferior, or reduce them to their sexual dimension. Sexist hate speech can occur online and offline through offensive comments about gender roles, appearance or sexuality, as well as supposed jokes and false compliments that use humour to humiliate and ridicule the target.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_b63eb0e9929946c80df3ee73__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
