    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID99",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_b63eb0e9929946c80df3ee73__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.2 immutable gender differences and gender stereotypes – Asserting immutable, natural or otherwise essential differences between men and women. In some cases, this could be in the form of using women’s traits to attack men. Most sexist jokes will fall into this category.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism includes beliefs, assertions, gestures or acts that express contempt toward someone based on sex or gender, treat that person as inferior, or reduce them to their sexual dimension. Sexist hate speech can occur online and offline through offensive comments about gender roles, appearance or sexuality, as well as supposed jokes and false compliments that use humour to humiliate and ridicule the target.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_b63eb0e9929946c80df3ee73__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
