    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID119",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_e019d89f6b53ae5b083f073d__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Awareness-raising initiatives should increase awareness and understanding among the general population, especially parents, of different forms of sexism, including “mansplaining,” and of how to prevent and respond to them. Such initiatives should also communicate the harm these forms of sexism generate for individuals and society, including girls and boys. Communication and awareness campaigns should address the links between sexism and violence against women and girls, alongside funding for organisations that support victims.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_e019d89f6b53ae5b083f073d__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
