    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID122",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_49613319de3797a9dfe9b3b0__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">I.B. Awareness-raising measures\n\n5. Mansplain (verb, informal): (of a man) to explain something to a woman in a manner regarded as condescending, patronising, overconfident, oversimplified, or which assumes the interlocutor has no knowledge of the topic.\n\nI.B.7. Promote a gender equality perspective, as well as the development of critical thinking for the countering of sexism in the content, language and illustrations of toys, comics, books, television, video and other games, online content and films, including pornography, which shape the attitudes, behaviour and identity of girls and boys.\n\nI.B.8. Promote and conduct regular awareness-raising campaigns on the construction of femininities and masculinities and what it means to be a woman/girl and a man/boy in contemporary society, for example through media, free public lectures and discussions.\n\nI.B.9. Encourage collaboration between professionals (for example journalists, educators, law-enforcement agents) and civil society organisations to determine and share good practices on preventing and combating sexism.\n\nI.B.10. Establish structures accessible to all, especially young people, to provide them with expert advice on how to prevent, combat and respond to sexism.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Mansplaining is defined as a man explaining something to a woman in a condescending, patronising, overconfident, or oversimplified manner, or in a way that assumes she has no knowledge of the topic. Awareness-raising measures promote gender equality perspectives and critical thinking to counter sexism in language, content, and illustrations, and campaigns address the construction of femininities and masculinities and what it means to be a woman or girl and a man or boy.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_49613319de3797a9dfe9b3b0__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
