        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.2 supporting systemic discrimination against women as a group – Expressing support for systemic discrimination of women as a group. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such discrimination.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Men’s groups and manosphere discourses use tactics such as deflecting from women’s rights issues, denying the validity of gender equality and women’s rights, minimizing their importance, flipping the narrative to centre men, and discrediting women’s rights activists. These tactics are paired with narratives that justify violence and hostility toward women, justify belittling women, portray men as victims of gender equality, justify the exclusion of women, and promote patriarchy and male privilege. Together, these patterns work to oppose gender equality, discredit feminists, and maintain a patriarchal agenda.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
